# Feature backends (clients/web)

Components never contain mock or sample data. Each product feature that can outrun FastAPI uses:

- `src/features/<feature>/repository.ts` — the only API the UI calls
- `src/features/<feature>/adapters/http.ts` — real `/api/backend/*` calls
- `src/features/<feature>/adapters/local.ts` — per-user, versioned localStorage (or IndexedDB), try/catch, used **only** when `NEXT_PUBLIC_FEATURE_<NAME>_BACKEND=local`

Selection lives in `src/config/feature-backends.ts`. Local-backed screens show a “Saved on this device” hint. Local keys are namespaced `juris:{userId}:{feature}` and must be cleared on sign-out (`clearLocalUserData`).

When an HTTP contract is not on FastAPI yet, document it in `docs/api-requests/<feature>.md` instead of inventing responses in components.
